## SEVERITY / VERDICT (the grading rule is decided HERE; apply it, do not re-argue it)
*Blocker:* a path beyond the one; a removed line other than the one parenthesis line (numstat not `10 1`); an `api/src` byte; the head blob not `447c5b79`; a non-ASCII byte, a person's name, a decision-card id, a `B###` token or a ticket key other than `HPSMPOC-354` in an added line or the commit message; a skip, sleep, retry loop, environment or provider gate, or a new `Task.Delay`; a change to `Slack`, `AssertHolds`, `Held`, `ArmOnly`, `DisarmOnly`, `Arm`, `Disarm`, a delay constant, the literal `1400`, or an existing test body or name (apart from the one comment line); any existing test red at the head on SQLite, or the whole project not equal to the base's (passed equal, failed 0, skipped equal), or names lost above 0 or added above 0; **a class row red, not `Passed`, skipped or missing on either run of Check 2/5 or on the SQL Server shard (Check 6)**; the head moved; a red or cancelled check-run; a CodeQL alert open on the head (either threshold), a missing analysis at the verdict, or an alert dismissed other than by the org; a textual conflict in Check 8; a secret.
*Major, class SAME (the class is "assertions added to one existing Api test row plus one comment parenthesis, tests only"):* **(M1) an added assertion that cannot do its job:** at the HEAD file, a mutant among Q, Q2, P3 (handler row), s1, s2, s3 that leaves a row green which that assertion exists to turn red, not shown equivalent by a run; **(M2) the rest-state claim falsified:** a failing rest-state assertion whose message does NOT name the static that is not at rest and its value; an accessor that reads a different static than it names (s5 survives); or a static left non-rest by any path of the head that makes another test red or order-dependent; **(M3)** a doc sentence the repository contradicts (the reworded parenthesis contradicts the earlier gate's cells, it says anything was measured on SQL Server, `SQL Server: not measured` is dropped, or a comment states a figure no record holds); **(M4) a product mutant of P1-P3 under which the existing staged test stays GREEN as well as the rows** (the whole class would not notice a stage losing its time).
*Major, class DIFFERENT:* a builder claim contradicted by measurement with a verdict consequence (28 in the class, 1993/0/13 as base, names lost 0 added 0, the mutant table: P3 handler row red, Q three rows red, s1-s3 red 3 of 3, 0 survivors, the rest-state message naming the static).
*Minor / Note (never a Major):* a comment that says more than its assertion proves (the "in any run order" sentence: the assertion reads state after the row's OWN `DisarmOnly`, so it pins that reset, not a leak from another test; Minor if it can be read as the latter, else Note); the **`finally { DisarmOnly(); }` line not pinned** (the builder disclosed it; the ticket's "records why a line cannot be pinned" branch; Note, with the L run); `RestState` omitting `_handlerHeld` and the three `Held` counters (reset by `Arm()` by design; Note); Wk2 equivalent (Note); P4 leaving staged test and rows green by construction while the caller-parts rows go red (the earlier gate's Note, re-measured); class seconds above the commission's figure; no green row near the floor (by design, the product owner's 2026-10-23 ruling); the caller-parts host and the `rest` stage not covered; the floor on SQL Server still UNMEASURED beyond the red side at 1400; H2 (1250) green on a stage (information); a margin mutant (H) that survives only on a stall of 100 ms or more; the unsigned commit; the PR title's ticket key; the PR body's trailer naming a different model than the commit's; bash/python/dotnet minor version differences from the runner.
*Where the line between Note and Major is unclear:* a thing that makes an assertion unable to fail, or makes another test depend on it, is at least Major SAME; a thing that changes only what a message or a comment says and stays true is a Note. Say which rule you applied for every finding.
